From: Marius Gehrmann <marius@gehrmann.solutions>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:29:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] m1n1: kboot: Reserve dcpext firmware on t8122

dcpext stays disabled on t8122 because dt_set_display() only calls
dt_reserve_dcpext_firmware() for t8112 and t602x. Add t8122 so the
dcpext ASC firmware is reserved and the node is enabled, as on t8112.

Like t8112, no separate dcpext carveout is added. On J613 the
firmware reservation already covers both dcpext regions with the same
PA and size: asc-firmware@103e0564000 (16 MiB) = region 74 and
asc-firmware@103e1564000 (3 MiB) = region 73 (dcpext __DATA). Its
iommu-addresses include the dart-dcpext vm-base (0x100_0000_0000);
a dcpext0 carveout from the region table only duplicates these
ranges, without the vm-base, and the kernel warns that they overlap.

Tested on MacBook Air M3 (J613) on current main, together with
AsahiLinux/linux PR #607: an external DP monitor on the left-back
USB-C port comes up at 1920x1080, and the overlap warning seen with
a dcpext0 carveout is gone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017YMqWu7A3VwEYtHaA1TusK
---
 m1n1/src/kboot.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/m1n1/src/kboot.c b/m1n1/src/kboot.c
index de9e3c7..f10bbee 100644
--- a/m1n1/src/kboot.c
+++ b/m1n1/src/kboot.c
@@ -2061,6 +2061,7 @@ static int dt_set_display(void)
      * if the reservation fails allowing basic operation with just dcp.
      */
     if (!fdt_node_check_compatible(dt, 0, "apple,t8112") ||
+        !fdt_node_check_compatible(dt, 0, "apple,t8122") ||
         !fdt_node_check_compatible(dt, 0, "apple,t6020") ||
         !fdt_node_check_compatible(dt, 0, "apple,t6021") ||
         !fdt_node_check_compatible(dt, 0, "apple,t6022"))
